      "title": "Handle the separate dummy object before computing a heap-array offset",
      "mechanism": "fake_entity_at returns &fake_dummy for an out-of-capacity stored slot. In the old-30fb red report case, resolve_report_target follows stored slot 36 after the declared capacity becomes 20, then calls get_local_entity_type on that dummy. entity_outside subtracts fake_entities from fake_dummy, which is a distinct static object, not an element or one-past pointer of that allocated array. This is undefined C pointer subtraction even though the accessor avoids the physical invalid entity read.",
      "consequence": "The test-only old-code red instrumentation is not fully defined C; ordinary ASan/UBSan success does not establish that this subtraction was valid. This is not a new production defect and does not negate the independently retained six native crashes or the corrected shipping guards.",
      "bounded_correction": "Return outside immediately when en == &fake_dummy before any subtraction. Preserve the current raw logs and recompute the bounded green, same old-30fb red and mutation harness evidence with that defined instrumentation; no physical formula, baseline, campaign input or native rerun needed."
    }
